# Adobe Creative Cloud — Global Engineering Standards

## Security (Non-Negotiable)
- NEVER log PII, credentials, API keys, or file paths containing user data
- All file uploads must validate MIME type against an allowlist before processing
- Sanitize all user-provided filenames before any filesystem operation
- Image data must not persist in memory beyond the request lifecycle
- No hardcoded secrets — use environment variables for all configuration

## Code Quality
- TypeScript strict mode required across all packages
- All exported functions must have JSDoc comments with @param and @returns
- Meaningful variable names — no single-letter variables outside loop iterators
- Maximum function length: 40 lines. Extract helpers beyond that threshold.

## Style
- camelCase for variables and functions, PascalCase for types and classes
- Barrel exports from each module's index.ts
- Prefer named exports over default exports

## Commit & PR Standards
- Use conventional commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, refactor:
- PR descriptions must include a "What changed" and "Why" section
